# grammar: v0 (unfrozen; AST normative)
#
# hello-world — the neutral teaching world that ships with dli.
#
# A tiny, generic setting (a river town — no particular genre or lore) that
# exercises the gentle surface subset end to end so a new author can learn dli
# without absorbing any one world's canon. It mirrors the shapes every later
# lane checks: an era spine (>=3 eras), events with a before-fact and a
# deliberately UNORDERED pair, places with an adjacency graph (>=6 edges),
# people, a thing, facts, states with since/until, and a question with options
# under a hypothesis. Provenance is this world's OWN decision list (d-0001..)
# — a solo writer's ledger, per 01-syntax §3.
scope hello-world

# --- the world's ledger: the decisions its citations rest on ------------------
# Declaring a decision is what lets `decided d-000n` carry authority rather than
# mint it (B1): a citation to an undeclared decision fails closed.
ratify d-0001
ratify d-0002
ratify d-0003
ratify d-0004
ratify d-0005
ratify d-0006
ratify d-0007

# --- world chronology: a totally-ordered era spine (>=3 eras) -----------------
era the-founding < the-growth-years < the-present   decided d-0001

# events carry era membership; WITHIN an era only `before` orders them
event the-ford-crossed  during the-founding      decided d-0002
event the-mill-built    during the-growth-years  decided d-0002
event the-bridge-raised during the-growth-years  decided d-0003
event the-spring-flood  during the-growth-years  proposed
event the-charter-signed during the-present      decided d-0007

# a declared intra-era order:
before the-mill-built -> the-bridge-raised        decided d-0003
# ...and a DELIBERATELY UNORDERED pair: the-spring-flood shares the-growth-years
# with the-mill-built but no before-fact orders them, so
# happens-before(the-spring-flood, the-mill-built) answers `unordered` — a
# first-class verdict, not a silent tie-break (03-time §1).

narration vantage the-present
# inert: the narrator looks back from the present; declaring an event here is a
# type error (03-time §1.iii).

# --- places and the adjacency graph (7 places, >=6 edges) ---------------------
place rivertown    "Rivertown"       decided d-0004
place the-market   "The Market"      decided d-0004
place the-mill     "The Mill"        decided d-0004
place the-bridge   "The Bridge"      decided d-0005
place the-commons  "The Commons"     decided d-0005
place the-orchard  "The Orchard"     decided d-0005
place the-north-road "The North Road" proposed

adjacent(rivertown, the-market)      decided d-0004
adjacent(the-market, the-mill)       decided d-0004
adjacent(the-mill, the-bridge)       decided d-0005
adjacent(rivertown, the-commons)     decided d-0005
adjacent(the-commons, the-orchard)   decided d-0005
adjacent(the-orchard, the-north-road) proposed
adjacent(the-north-road, the-bridge) proposed

# --- people, a thing, and facts -----------------------------------------------
person edda    "Edda the Miller"     decided d-0006
person tomas   "Tomas Warden"        decided d-0006
thing the-town-ledger "The Town Ledger" decided d-0007

fact edda  lives-in rivertown        decided d-0006
fact tomas keeps    the-commons      decided d-0006

# --- states: facts acquire validity spans (a two-era case) --------------------
state the-mill.wheel = idle    until the-mill-built   decided d-0002
state the-mill.wheel = turning since the-mill-built   decided d-0002
# idle UNTIL the mill is built and turning SINCE it: a founding-era flashback
# checks clean AND the present checks clean, because the two claims hold over
# disjoint spans (03-time §2). No false contradiction between them.

# --- an open fork: a question with options under a hypothesis ------------------
hypothesis h-ledger "the town ledger was kept at the mill, not the market"

question who-keeps-the-ledger "Who keeps the town ledger?"
  option tomas implies keeps(tomas, the-town-ledger)
  option edda  implies keeps(edda, the-town-ledger)   assumes h-ledger
# proposed-first: neither option is canon until a ruling; the question is a
# tracked debt, not a blank (01-syntax §4).
